1
00:00:01,033 --> 00:00:07,933
["YOU'RE MY FAVORITE SONG"
BY PRINCESS ALIYAH]

2
00:00:08,267 --> 00:00:11,133
<i>Previously on
You're My Favorite Song...</i>

3
00:00:11,267 --> 00:00:14,667
<i>Today, marks 16 years
since Celestine disappeared.</i>

4
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:17,233
<i> It's not wrong...</i>

5
00:00:17,367 --> 00:00:19,967
<i>to keep hoping that even now...</i>

6
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:23,800
<i>she's still alive
and I'll find my child.</i>

7
00:00:23,933 --> 00:00:26,133
<i> Isn't Enrico alone in life?</i>

8
00:00:26,267 --> 00:00:28,967
<i>So technically, if something
happens to him,</i>

9
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:30,800
<i> all his wealth will go to you.</i>

10
00:00:30,933 --> 00:00:33,267
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

11
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:36,700
<i>Are you suggesting
we kill Enrico?</i>

12
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:42,900
<i>Her anger toward us is intense.</i>

13
00:00:43,033 --> 00:00:45,100
<i>I want our family to truly
reconcile,</i>

14
00:00:45,233 --> 00:00:48,400
<i> a genuine reconciliation.</i>

15
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:50,000
<i> Here's the payment.</i>

16
00:00:50,867 --> 00:00:52,267
<i> I'll add more,</i>

17
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:54,500
<i>just make sure you do
your job well.</i>

18
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,500
<i> Leave it to us, Miss Serina.</i>

19
00:00:57,633 --> 00:00:59,533
<i>Their grand opening
won't happen.</i>

20
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,100
<i> Just make sure of it.</i>

21
00:01:02,233 --> 00:01:05,833
<i>Make sure you ruin
Gran Vista Resort.</i>

22
00:01:05,967 --> 00:01:07,067
<i> Charm,</i>

23
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:08,367
<i> your test paper.</i>

24
00:01:08,533 --> 00:01:09,567
<i> Congrats,</i>

25
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:11,100
<i> 85 out of 100.</i>

26
00:01:11,233 --> 00:01:12,567
<i> We got the same score.</i>

27
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:15,233
<i> Thank you.</i>

28
00:01:15,367 --> 00:01:17,300
<i>Why do you keep looking
at Charm?</i>

29
00:01:17,433 --> 00:01:18,600
<i> Do you have a crush on her?</i>

30
00:01:18,733 --> 00:01:21,467
<i>Yeah.
[CHUCKLES]</i>

31
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:23,167
<i> No, but...</i>

32
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:24,333
<i> That's not important.</i>

33
00:01:24,467 --> 00:01:27,533
<i>What matters is,
aside from Calix,</i>

34
00:01:27,667 --> 00:01:30,133
<i>she's someone you shouldn't go
up against.</i>

35
00:01:30,267 --> 00:01:32,633
<i> I'm not afraid of you, Calix.</i>

36
00:01:32,767 --> 00:01:33,700
<i> Wrong answer.</i>

37
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:37,000
<i> Because you should be.</i>

38
00:01:37,133 --> 00:01:38,000
<i> Do it, Calix.</i>

39
00:01:38,133 --> 00:01:39,033
<i> Punch her.</i>

40
00:01:39,167 --> 00:01:40,800
<i> Yeah, she deserves it.</i>

41
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:50,800
["YOU'RE MY FAVORITE SONG"
BY PRINCESS ALIYAH]

42
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:22,800
Hi, Miss Roxanne.

43
00:02:22,933 --> 00:02:23,900
Yes.

44
00:02:24,033 --> 00:02:26,367
Thank you so much
for accommodating me.

45
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:28,633
I really wanted to own
a piece

46
00:02:28,767 --> 00:02:30,000
from your collection.

47
00:02:30,133 --> 00:02:33,267
Having you as a client
is a privilege.

48
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:36,767
That's why I personally
came to your mansion.

49
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:38,867
[CHUCKLES]
May I see it?

50
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,167
Sure.

51
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:51,033
Anyway, you know
I prefer things simple.

52
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:53,500
I like simple designs,

53
00:02:53,633 --> 00:02:54,600
nothing flashy.

54
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:58,333
This is the one I wanted.

55
00:02:58,467 --> 00:02:59,567
There, it's simple.

56
00:02:59,700 --> 00:03:01,533
Yeah.

57
00:03:01,667 --> 00:03:05,067
But that one has
already been sold.

58
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:07,233
I only made one like that,

59
00:03:07,367 --> 00:03:09,333
it's very exclusive.

60
00:03:11,533 --> 00:03:13,400
That's too bad.
[CHUCKLES]

61
00:03:13,533 --> 00:03:15,067
Actually,

62
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:16,900
the person who bought that...

63
00:03:17,033 --> 00:03:18,833
is someone dear to you.

64
00:03:18,967 --> 00:03:20,300
- Really?
- Yes.

65
00:03:20,433 --> 00:03:21,400
Who?

66
00:03:21,567 --> 00:03:22,833
Your wife,

67
00:03:22,967 --> 00:03:25,333
Miss Serina.

68
00:03:25,467 --> 00:03:29,800
She specifically asked me
for men's jewelry.

69
00:03:29,933 --> 00:03:31,667
[ENRICO CHUCKLES]

70
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:33,367
Looks like it's not
a surprise anymore.

71
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:34,600
You already told me.

72
00:03:34,733 --> 00:03:38,600
I'm sure she's going to give
that to you as a gift.

73
00:03:38,733 --> 00:03:40,133
But...

74
00:03:40,267 --> 00:03:43,400
don't tell her I told you, Sir.

75
00:03:44,833 --> 00:03:46,533
Of course.

76
00:03:46,667 --> 00:03:47,533
Thank you.

77
00:03:47,667 --> 00:03:48,733
Take a look.

78
00:03:48,867 --> 00:03:50,167
Yes, it's beautiful.

79
00:03:58,333 --> 00:03:59,833
Happy anniversary.

80
00:04:01,433 --> 00:04:03,467
Thank you, Serina.
[CHUCKLES]

81
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:05,600
Here.

82
00:04:07,367 --> 00:04:09,133
This is for you.

83
00:04:09,267 --> 00:04:10,767
- It's all I could afford.
- Thank you.

84
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:14,100
I used to earn more
at the casino than now,

85
00:04:14,233 --> 00:04:15,467
working as your driver.

86
00:04:16,433 --> 00:04:17,700
[CLICKS TONGUE]
Come on,

87
00:04:17,833 --> 00:04:19,800
what matters
is that we're together.

88
00:04:19,933 --> 00:04:23,467
We can be together
without Enrico ever knowing.

89
00:04:26,133 --> 00:04:27,100
So, did you like my gift?

90
00:04:27,233 --> 00:04:28,333
Of course.

91
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:30,167
It's beautiful.

92
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:32,967
You know, that cost me
almost a million pesos.

93
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:34,733
But I made sure
it looked ordinary

94
00:04:34,867 --> 00:04:37,833
so Enrico wouldn't
suspect anything.

95
00:04:37,967 --> 00:04:39,900
- Wow.
- It suits you.

96
00:04:41,233 --> 00:04:42,333
Thank you.

97
00:04:45,367 --> 00:04:47,667
- [SMOOCHES]
- Thank you, Baby.

98
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:48,900
You're welcome.

99
00:04:50,833 --> 00:04:51,833
It's beautiful.

100
00:04:55,067 --> 00:04:57,067
It suits me perfectly.

101
00:04:57,200 --> 00:04:58,733
[CHUCKLES]
It really does.

102
00:04:58,867 --> 00:04:59,767
[CHUCKLES]

103
00:05:01,367 --> 00:05:03,200
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]

104
00:05:03,333 --> 00:05:06,600
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

105
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:11,233
Good thing there's no staff
around right now.

106
00:05:11,367 --> 00:05:14,167
Well then, let's turn
Gran Vista into "Gone Vista."

107
00:05:14,300 --> 00:05:15,467
[LAUGHS]
Gone Vista.

108
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:16,500
- Let's go.
- Hurry! Destroy everything,

109
00:05:16,633 --> 00:05:18,367
so Miss Serina will be pleased.

110
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:20,700
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

111
00:05:20,833 --> 00:05:21,767
I'll take this.

112
00:05:23,567 --> 00:05:27,267
You know, if we work together,
you'll get more done.

113
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:29,200
- How are we going to sell that?
- Dad, help me out.

114
00:05:29,333 --> 00:05:33,200
- Of course.
- We can sell a lot today.

115
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:36,300
- [THUDS]
- [BOTTLES CLATTER]

116
00:05:38,233 --> 00:05:39,133
Do you hear that?

117
00:05:39,267 --> 00:05:41,433
[OBJECTS CLATTERING]

118
00:05:47,233 --> 00:05:49,433
[THUMPING]

119
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:53,933
- There it is again.
- Oh, no.

120
00:05:54,067 --> 00:05:55,933
What's that?

121
00:05:56,067 --> 00:05:56,967
Wait a second.

122
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:03,200
Dad, wait, I'm coming with you.

123
00:06:03,333 --> 00:06:07,567
[GRIPPING MUSIC PLAYING]

124
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,400
Hey!

125
00:06:17,533 --> 00:06:19,933
- Who are you?
- Hey! What are you doing?

126
00:06:20,067 --> 00:06:21,433
- Hey! Dad.
- Wait!

127
00:06:21,567 --> 00:06:22,633
- Hey! Where are you going?
- Wait! Wait!

128
00:06:22,767 --> 00:06:23,833
- Where are you going?
- Just wait!

129
00:06:23,967 --> 00:06:25,467
Where are you going?
Why did you destroy our resort?

130
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:27,333
- Yeah, who are you?
- Let go of me.

131
00:06:28,933 --> 00:06:30,000
Who are you with?

132
00:06:30,133 --> 00:06:31,967
- [NICO GRUNTS]
- [XAVI THUDS]

133
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:33,000
Dad!

134
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:36,967
Dad, Dad!

135
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:38,367
My child.

136
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:39,700
Dad, wait.

137
00:06:39,833 --> 00:06:41,067
[XAVI GROANS]
Dad, what's happening?

138
00:06:41,233 --> 00:06:43,067
Dad, Dad!

139
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:44,200
Dad!

140
00:06:44,333 --> 00:06:45,800
Dad!

141
00:06:45,933 --> 00:06:47,000
Dad!

142
00:06:49,267 --> 00:06:51,267
Dad!

143
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:52,533
Help us!

144
00:06:52,667 --> 00:06:54,633
Dad!

145
00:06:54,767 --> 00:06:56,600
Dad, Dad.

146
00:07:13,533 --> 00:07:14,300
Do it, Calix.

147
00:07:14,467 --> 00:07:15,367
Punch her.

148
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:17,033
- Yeah, she deserves it.
- Come on.

149
00:07:17,167 --> 00:07:18,633
Go, go.

150
00:07:20,033 --> 00:07:23,900
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

151
00:07:24,033 --> 00:07:25,033
- Hey!
- Hey!

152
00:07:25,167 --> 00:07:26,100
Hey!

153
00:07:26,233 --> 00:07:28,733
- Hey! My bag!
- For three!

154
00:07:28,867 --> 00:07:30,467
- [BAG THUDS]
- [CAR BRAKE SQUEALS]

155
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:32,300
What was that?

156
00:07:32,433 --> 00:07:34,333
Something fell.

157
00:07:34,467 --> 00:07:35,967
You're crazy, Calix!

158
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:37,833
Bang!

159
00:07:37,967 --> 00:07:40,633
Oh, my god.

160
00:07:40,767 --> 00:07:42,400
- Three!
- You're insane!

161
00:07:42,533 --> 00:07:43,800
<i> That was far.</i>

162
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:46,800
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

163
00:07:46,933 --> 00:07:48,867
<i> For three.</i>

164
00:07:52,933 --> 00:07:55,100
- [KICK LANDS]
- [GUITAR THUDS]

165
00:07:55,233 --> 00:07:56,233
My guitar!

166
00:07:56,367 --> 00:07:57,633
Let's go after them!

167
00:07:57,767 --> 00:07:59,800
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

168
00:07:59,933 --> 00:08:00,667
Hey, Zion!

169
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:02,567
- Come here!
- Hurry!

170
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,500
Move faster!

171
00:08:07,633 --> 00:08:09,667
[ADIE AND CHARM LAUGHING]

172
00:08:11,867 --> 00:08:12,833
I'll check.

173
00:08:14,867 --> 00:08:17,833
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

174
00:08:21,233 --> 00:08:23,000
Miguel, let's go.

175
00:08:23,133 --> 00:08:24,867
Someone might see us.

176
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,000
Wait.

177
00:08:29,167 --> 00:08:30,000
This bag...

178
00:08:31,233 --> 00:08:32,533
I know this bag.

179
00:08:32,667 --> 00:08:35,933
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

180
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:44,600
There! Someone took my bag,
Zion.

181
00:08:50,467 --> 00:08:51,867
Miguel, let's go.

182
00:09:00,067 --> 00:09:01,433
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

183
00:09:01,733 --> 00:09:03,333
Miguel, let's go.

184
00:09:03,467 --> 00:09:05,500
Someone might see us.

185
00:09:11,333 --> 00:09:13,167
There! Someone took my bag,
Zion.

186
00:09:19,167 --> 00:09:20,500
Miguel, let's go.

187
00:09:22,867 --> 00:09:25,200
He has my bag, Zion, let's go!

188
00:09:25,333 --> 00:09:26,833
He didn't actually take it.

189
00:09:26,967 --> 00:09:29,033
He probably just moved it
so it wouldn't get run over.

190
00:09:32,467 --> 00:09:34,700
That was kind of him.

191
00:09:34,833 --> 00:09:36,533
Too bad I didn't get
to thank him.

192
00:09:43,433 --> 00:09:44,167
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
Calix is there,

193
00:09:44,300 --> 00:09:46,333
we need to hide.

194
00:09:46,467 --> 00:09:47,600
There!

195
00:09:47,733 --> 00:09:48,767
- There they are!
- Hurry, hurry! Run!

196
00:09:48,900 --> 00:09:50,533
- Where?
- Go after them.

197
00:09:54,033 --> 00:09:55,600
They're dead meat again
because of Calix.

198
00:09:55,733 --> 00:09:56,667
There they go again.

199
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:58,100
They're in trouble
with Calix again.

200
00:09:58,233 --> 00:10:00,800
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

201
00:10:10,933 --> 00:10:11,800
Tyrone.

202
00:10:11,933 --> 00:10:14,300
- Sir.
- I'll take my wife to work.

203
00:10:14,433 --> 00:10:17,833
It's been a while since
I've driven her to work myself.

204
00:10:19,233 --> 00:10:20,633
Take the day off.

205
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:23,100
All right, Sir, that's fine.

206
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:25,433
The keys.

207
00:10:25,567 --> 00:10:26,567
Ah, right.

208
00:10:27,833 --> 00:10:31,233
Sir.
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

209
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:35,933
Your bracelet is beautiful.

210
00:10:36,067 --> 00:10:37,533
That's expensive, isn't it?

211
00:10:37,667 --> 00:10:39,167
Where did you get it?

212
00:10:39,300 --> 00:10:40,867
It was a gift, Sir.

213
00:10:42,667 --> 00:10:43,733
From who?

214
00:10:45,900 --> 00:10:47,067
My girlfriend, Sir.

215
00:10:50,467 --> 00:10:51,533
I'll go ahead now.

216
00:10:51,667 --> 00:10:52,733
All right.

217
00:10:58,600 --> 00:10:59,600
<i> Nanny.</i>

218
00:10:59,733 --> 00:11:02,533
Love, where's my driver?

219
00:11:02,667 --> 00:11:03,700
Oh, thank you.

220
00:11:03,833 --> 00:11:05,900
I gave him the day off.

221
00:11:06,033 --> 00:11:07,367
So...

222
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:08,700
who's going to drive for me?

223
00:11:08,867 --> 00:11:10,733
I'm running late for my meeting.

224
00:11:10,867 --> 00:11:12,033
[CAR DOOR SLAMS]

225
00:11:13,467 --> 00:11:15,633
What the heck is your problem?

226
00:11:18,567 --> 00:11:20,800
Tell me the truth.

227
00:11:20,933 --> 00:11:22,567
Are you having an affair
with Tyrone?

228
00:11:22,700 --> 00:11:26,900
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

229
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:38,633
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

230
00:11:46,533 --> 00:11:48,067
[BEVERLY SNIFFLES]

231
00:11:56,433 --> 00:11:58,767
[BEVERLY SOBS]

232
00:12:07,167 --> 00:12:08,067
Dad...

233
00:12:09,233 --> 00:12:11,067
Hold on, Dad.

234
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,700
You can't leave us yet.

235
00:12:17,833 --> 00:12:20,100
You can't leave us behind.

236
00:12:21,433 --> 00:12:23,100
Angel will be heartbroken.

237
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:28,833
And we haven't finished
your bucket list yet.

238
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:33,333
Serina is still angry at us.

239
00:12:35,233 --> 00:12:37,700
Dad, wake up.

240
00:12:39,767 --> 00:12:41,100
[BEVERLY SNIFFLES]

241
00:12:45,667 --> 00:12:48,033
[BEVERLY SOBBING, SNIFFLES]

242
00:12:57,833 --> 00:12:59,267
<i> Excuse me.</i>

243
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:03,900
Hello, Ma'am. How are you, Sir?

244
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:04,833
Doc,

245
00:13:04,967 --> 00:13:08,100
how is he? How is my father?

246
00:13:08,233 --> 00:13:12,167
Ma'am, aside from his heightened
emotions due to anger,

247
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:14,567
your father has fluid
in his lungs

248
00:13:14,700 --> 00:13:17,100
which caused tightness
in his chest.

249
00:13:17,233 --> 00:13:21,133
But we are doing everything
we can so please don't worry.

250
00:13:22,433 --> 00:13:25,367
If you need anything,
Ma'am, I'm here.

251
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:29,000
Let's just wait for the rest
of his test results.

252
00:13:29,133 --> 00:13:30,133
Yes.

253
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:31,267
Thank you, Doc.

254
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:32,300
All right.

255
00:13:33,533 --> 00:13:36,900
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

256
00:13:38,967 --> 00:13:40,767
[BEVERLY SNIFFLES]

257
00:13:44,767 --> 00:13:46,300
[SNIFFLES]

258
00:13:48,267 --> 00:13:49,833
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

259
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:53,833
I need to call Angel.

260
00:13:59,233 --> 00:14:00,800
Stay strong.

261
00:14:00,933 --> 00:14:01,833
Calm down.

262
00:14:01,967 --> 00:14:04,167
[SNIFFLES]

263
00:14:04,300 --> 00:14:05,300
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

264
00:14:06,967 --> 00:14:08,367
Angel, hurry!

265
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:12,900
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

266
00:14:19,133 --> 00:14:21,600
Angel, here, here, hurry!

267
00:14:21,733 --> 00:14:22,833
Hurry!

268
00:14:22,967 --> 00:14:24,333
[DOOR CLOSES]

269
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,367
Get everyone out of here.

270
00:14:29,533 --> 00:14:30,533
- Hey! Get out.
- Move!

271
00:14:30,667 --> 00:14:32,233
- I said move! Out!
- Poncy.

272
00:14:32,367 --> 00:14:33,800
- Make sure no one comes up.
- Boss.

273
00:14:33,933 --> 00:14:36,700
I'm sure they're hiding
in these rooms.

274
00:14:36,833 --> 00:14:39,067
We'll go through every room
and door here.

275
00:14:39,200 --> 00:14:41,400
- All right.
- Until I find them.

276
00:14:41,533 --> 00:14:43,333
Especially that idiot Zion.

277
00:14:45,867 --> 00:14:47,667
Zion, what are we going to do?

278
00:14:47,800 --> 00:14:49,567
[PANTING]
Just wait.

279
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:52,100
Stay quiet for now.

280
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:57,433
Come on, come out already!

281
00:14:58,633 --> 00:15:00,167
There's no use in hiding.

282
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:02,233
- [DIALING]
- [EXHALES DEEPLY]

283
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:07,467
[LINE RINGING]

284
00:15:09,933 --> 00:15:12,600
[CELLPHONE RINGS]

285
00:15:13,833 --> 00:15:15,300
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

286
00:15:15,433 --> 00:15:17,867
[RINGING CONTINUES]

287
00:15:19,733 --> 00:15:22,300
[DIALING]

288
00:15:22,433 --> 00:15:24,333
[LINE RINGING]

289
00:15:29,433 --> 00:15:31,267
[CELLPHONE RINGING]

290
00:15:33,667 --> 00:15:34,867
There.

291
00:15:35,033 --> 00:15:36,533
I can't believe
they're that stupid.

292
00:15:36,667 --> 00:15:38,567
[TENSE MUSIC]

293
00:15:40,667 --> 00:15:42,533
[PHONE VIBRATES]

294
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:44,900
It's Mama Bebe.

295
00:15:45,633 --> 00:15:47,167
I wonder why she's calling.

296
00:15:48,333 --> 00:15:49,067
Got you.

297
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:51,300
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

298
00:15:53,467 --> 00:15:55,133
[LINE RINGING]

299
00:15:55,267 --> 00:15:57,333
<i>We're sorry,
the number you have reached</i>

300
00:15:57,467 --> 00:15:58,467
<i> is not in service.</i>

301
00:15:58,600 --> 00:16:01,967
She might still be in class.
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

302
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:03,533
I'll just message her.

303
00:16:03,667 --> 00:16:05,567
[TYPING]

304
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:16,267
Angel, I think they heard us.

305
00:16:16,567 --> 00:16:18,900
Okay, here's what we'll do,
when I open the door,

306
00:16:19,033 --> 00:16:20,733
I'll handle distracting them.

307
00:16:20,867 --> 00:16:22,300
You just run as fast
as you can, okay?

308
00:16:26,967 --> 00:16:28,467
[ANGEL SOBBING]
Angel.

309
00:16:32,267 --> 00:16:34,100
My grandfather,
Grandfather Xavi,

310
00:16:34,233 --> 00:16:36,200
is in the hospital, Zion.

311
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:38,533
What?

312
00:16:41,767 --> 00:16:43,600
Got you.
[LAUGHS]

313
00:16:55,933 --> 00:16:57,633
Angel?

314
00:16:58,667 --> 00:17:00,367
I haven't even done anything
to you yet.

315
00:17:01,533 --> 00:17:02,567
Why are you crying?

316
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:13,400
[ZION GRUNTS]

317
00:17:13,533 --> 00:17:14,933
- Angel, run now, hurry!
- Hey! Let go of me!

318
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:15,900
Hey!
[OVERLAPPING SHOUTING]

319
00:17:16,033 --> 00:17:17,467
Move aside!

320
00:17:17,833 --> 00:17:19,533
- Let me go!
- Angel, hurry!

321
00:17:19,667 --> 00:17:21,200
Don't move, Zion!

322
00:17:23,267 --> 00:17:24,500
Can you stop messing with Angel?

323
00:17:24,633 --> 00:17:26,633
She has something important
to attend to.

324
00:17:26,767 --> 00:17:28,667
Like we care.

325
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:30,267
You've got some nerve.

326
00:17:35,033 --> 00:17:36,400
I could let Angel go.

327
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:39,467
But you...

328
00:17:41,167 --> 00:17:42,400
you're an idiot.

329
00:17:43,333 --> 00:17:44,767
You ruined my guitar.

330
00:17:45,833 --> 00:17:47,100
And you're going to pay for it.

331
00:17:53,867 --> 00:17:56,133
Oh, we're in trouble again.

332
00:18:02,667 --> 00:18:03,800
Tell me the truth.

333
00:18:04,933 --> 00:18:06,433
Are you having an affair
with Tyrone?

334
00:18:06,567 --> 00:18:08,433
[TENSE MUSIC]

335
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:12,000
[SCOFFS]

336
00:18:12,133 --> 00:18:13,767
What kind of nonsense
are you talking about?

337
00:18:15,867 --> 00:18:17,367
The bracelet Tyrone
is wearing...

338
00:18:18,933 --> 00:18:20,367
you gave that to him,
didn't you?

339
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:21,767
You bought it from Roxanne?

340
00:18:21,933 --> 00:18:23,633
[TENSE MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

341
00:18:23,767 --> 00:18:25,067
And who told you that?

342
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:26,933
Roxanne herself.

343
00:18:27,433 --> 00:18:30,933
I was supposed to buy it,
but she said you got it first.

344
00:18:31,067 --> 00:18:34,400
And I thought you were buying it
for me.

345
00:18:34,533 --> 00:18:36,400
Turns out, you gave it
to Tyrone.

346
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:44,367
Enrico, is that really
how low you think of me?

347
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:48,233
You think I'm having an affair
with my driver?

348
00:18:48,833 --> 00:18:52,833
Then why would you buy Tyrone
a bracelet worth 700,000 pesos?

349
00:18:56,367 --> 00:18:58,367
He just asked me to buy it
for him.

350
00:18:58,500 --> 00:19:00,433
Tyrone has a girlfriend
in the U.S.,

351
00:19:00,567 --> 00:19:04,500
an old woman who gives him money
that he met at a casino.

352
00:19:04,633 --> 00:19:08,200
And she wants him to buy jewelry
for himself

353
00:19:08,333 --> 00:19:09,500
because it's their anniversary.

354
00:19:09,633 --> 00:19:11,633
And I just helped him
to get an expensive one.

355
00:19:14,133 --> 00:19:15,333
Is that true?

356
00:19:15,467 --> 00:19:17,800
Yes. I can even introduce you
to her if you want.

357
00:19:17,933 --> 00:19:19,367
- That won't be necessary.
- I'll call Tyrone.

358
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:25,233
You know, I can't believe you,
Enrico.

359
00:19:26,133 --> 00:19:27,100
[SIGHS]

360
00:19:27,233 --> 00:19:29,167
After everything
that we've been through,

361
00:19:29,333 --> 00:19:30,833
even when you almost took
your own life

362
00:19:30,967 --> 00:19:32,200
after losing everything,

363
00:19:32,333 --> 00:19:34,833
I was there by your side.

364
00:19:34,967 --> 00:19:37,000
And despite everything
that I did,

365
00:19:37,133 --> 00:19:38,667
you still have the nerve
to accuse me

366
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:41,133
that I'm having an affair?

367
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,200
How dare you think of me
like that?

368
00:19:46,767 --> 00:19:47,767
Serina.

369
00:19:47,900 --> 00:19:48,800
Serina, I'm sorry.

370
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:02,833
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

371
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,667
Can we take a photo?

372
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:06,700
[UPBEAT MUSIC]

373
00:20:08,467 --> 00:20:09,433
Jacob.

374
00:20:11,333 --> 00:20:14,667
Do you think that bag
could belong to Angel?

375
00:20:17,433 --> 00:20:19,567
A lot of people have that kind
of bag, Miguel.

376
00:20:19,700 --> 00:20:22,500
And besides, isn't Angel
from Manila?

377
00:20:23,067 --> 00:20:25,300
Why would she be in a school
here in Solmera City?

378
00:20:28,933 --> 00:20:30,167
Anyway...

379
00:20:31,633 --> 00:20:32,467
Thank you.

380
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:34,833
I'll be busking later
outside Brighton Bay.

381
00:20:36,267 --> 00:20:37,433
If she's there...

382
00:20:39,133 --> 00:20:40,333
I'll see her.

383
00:20:41,033 --> 00:20:42,467
<i> Thank you.</i>

384
00:20:46,700 --> 00:20:47,733
[JACOB CHUCKLES]

385
00:20:50,300 --> 00:20:53,200
<i>Miguel, Miguel, look over here.</i>

386
00:20:57,267 --> 00:20:59,333
Thank you.
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

387
00:21:04,933 --> 00:21:06,000
Miguel...
[CHUCKLES]

388
00:21:06,133 --> 00:21:07,467
you seem distracted.

389
00:21:08,300 --> 00:21:10,400
Please focus on your fans.

390
00:21:10,533 --> 00:21:12,500
Fix yourself. Smile, engage.

391
00:21:12,633 --> 00:21:15,700
They might think
you're being aloof.

392
00:21:15,833 --> 00:21:17,767
Yes, Dad. Sorry.

393
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:25,400
[FANS CHEERING]

394
00:21:25,533 --> 00:21:26,967
["IKAW LANG ('DI KO MASABI)"
BY HEATH JORNALES]

395
00:21:27,100 --> 00:21:28,967
[FANS CHEERING, WHOOPING]

396
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:32,333
Siklab! Siklab! Siklab!

397
00:21:32,467 --> 00:21:35,600
Siklab! Siklab! Siklab!
Siklab! Siklab!

398
00:21:36,300 --> 00:21:44,633
[FANS CHEERING, WHOOPING]

399
00:21:55,967 --> 00:21:57,100
Gino.

400
00:21:57,233 --> 00:21:58,933
Sir, do we have somewhere to go?

401
00:21:59,267 --> 00:22:00,900
I want you to follow my wife.

402
00:22:02,067 --> 00:22:03,767
Watch her movements closely.

403
00:22:03,900 --> 00:22:06,600
See if she's doing anything
behind my back.

404
00:22:06,967 --> 00:22:08,633
Babe, what are you doing?

405
00:22:08,967 --> 00:22:10,633
Someone might see us here.

406
00:22:11,467 --> 00:22:13,467
This is a CCTV blind spot.

407
00:22:13,867 --> 00:22:15,667
I know every corner
of this mansion.

408
00:22:18,400 --> 00:22:20,733
You'll undergo chemotherapy.

409
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:22,000
I'll help.

410
00:22:22,133 --> 00:22:24,333
I'll find a way to earn money.

411
00:22:24,467 --> 00:22:26,533
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC]

412
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:32,300
Zion, thank you.

413
00:22:32,433 --> 00:22:34,433
["YOU'RE MY FAVORITE SONG"
INSTRUMENTAL]

414
00:22:47,967 --> 00:22:51,100
I want you to be Calix's
new partner

415
00:22:51,267 --> 00:22:53,133
for the Regional Quizcon,

416
00:22:53,267 --> 00:22:55,733
which will be happening
tomorrow.

417
00:22:55,867 --> 00:22:59,867
The prize money
will be 35,000 pesos.

418
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:01,900
And if you guys win,

419
00:23:02,033 --> 00:23:04,600
you will share this
between the two of you.

420
00:23:06,333 --> 00:23:07,833
Don't you dare accept it.

421
00:23:07,967 --> 00:23:10,600
If you do,
I'll make your life hell.

422
00:23:13,767 --> 00:23:15,733
["YOU'RE MY FAVORITE SONG"
BY PRINCESS ALIYAH]

423
00:23:16,567 --> 00:23:17,867
If it's okay with you,

424
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,333
I can lift you up.

425
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:22,567
You seem familiar.
